1
00:00:25,043 --> 00:00:26,223
How about you?

2
00:00:26,443 --> 00:00:27,561
Feel like fighting?

3
00:00:28,243 --> 00:00:29,463
No thanks, pal.

4
00:00:29,963 --> 00:00:34,081
My magic skill's gonna reach 900
soon, so I'd rather not die just yet.

5
00:00:34,563 --> 00:00:35,940
At least you're honest about it.

6
00:00:36,023 --> 00:00:37,199
How about you, miss?

7
00:00:39,563 --> 00:00:40,760
Guess I'll pass, too.

8
00:00:40,843 --> 00:00:43,223
But next time, you're going down! Oh.

9
00:00:43,583 --> 00:00:47,054
Then next time, I'll make sure
to bring more friends along.

10
00:01:29,023 --> 00:01:32,663
I'm not sure if it's the future.

11
00:01:33,183 --> 00:01:35,943
I don't have to say goodbye.

12
00:01:36,403 --> 00:01:38,579
I'm not sure if I'm going to hear it.

13
00:01:39,143 --> 00:01:41,363
I'm not sure if I'm going to hear it.

14
00:01:43,523 --> 00:01:45,823
I'm not sure if it's a lie.

15
00:02:18,823 --> 00:02:19,653
You

16
00:02:24,863 --> 00:02:25,693
Hey,

17
00:02:25,776 --> 00:02:28,100
what's up with those
flames there remain lights

18
00:02:28,183 --> 00:02:30,654
the players who killed can still hear you?

19
00:02:33,663 --> 00:02:38,960
Okay, now we can talk so what do you
want you want me to thank you run away,

20
00:02:39,043 --> 00:02:40,903
or do you want to fight?

21
00:02:42,063 --> 00:02:42,893
Hmm.

22
00:02:42,976 --> 00:02:44,560
If we break down what just happened,

23
00:02:44,643 --> 00:02:47,700
it's one of those knight in shining
armor-saves-the-princess moments.

24
00:02:47,783 --> 00:02:48,613
Huh?

25
00:02:48,696 --> 00:02:51,120
You could burst into tears
and throw your arms around me.

26
00:02:51,203 --> 00:02:52,603
Oh, piss off, loser!

27
00:02:53,663 --> 00:02:55,075
Nah, I was just kidding.

28
00:02:56,743 --> 00:02:57,573
No way!

29
00:02:57,923 --> 00:03:01,603
It won't let her do that!
Watch it! Stay out of sight!

30
00:03:01,963 --> 00:03:04,620
Mommy and me are the only
ones allowed to hug Daddy!

31
00:03:04,703 --> 00:03:05,643
Wait, Daddy?

32
00:03:06,363 --> 00:03:08,120
What? Nothing. No.

33
00:03:08,203 --> 00:03:09,783
No way.

34
00:03:10,123 --> 00:03:12,241
Is that one of those private pixies?

35
00:03:13,123 --> 00:03:14,983
Sort of, I guess.

36
00:03:16,003 --> 00:03:16,863
Mm-hmm.

37
00:03:17,643 --> 00:03:22,525
Then how about you tell me what a Spriggan
like you is doing wandering around here?

38
00:03:22,643 --> 00:03:24,723
I guess I got lost.

39
00:03:28,583 --> 00:03:30,583
How could you get that lost?

40
00:03:31,083 --> 00:03:33,259
Spriggan territory's way to the east.

41
00:03:33,563 --> 00:03:34,863
God, you're weird.

42
00:03:39,963 --> 00:03:41,845
Anyway, thank you for saving me.

43
00:03:41,943 --> 00:03:43,900
I guess I should introduce myself.

44
00:03:43,983 --> 00:03:45,630
I'm Leafa, nice to meet you.

45
00:03:45,843 --> 00:03:48,343
I'm Kirito, and this is Yui.

46
00:03:53,643 --> 00:03:55,643
Okay, then, Kirito.

47
00:03:56,083 --> 00:03:57,730
Do you have any plans today?

48
00:03:57,983 --> 00:04:02,243
I mean, because if you don't, I
can buy you a drink as thanks.

49
00:04:02,503 --> 00:04:04,760
A drink sounds awesome,
and if you don't mind,

50
00:04:04,843 --> 00:04:06,520
I'd like to pick your
brain about some stuff.

51
00:04:06,603 --> 00:04:08,403
Like, what kind of stuff?

52
00:04:08,743 --> 00:04:10,331
Just more about this world.

53
00:04:10,503 --> 00:04:13,083
And especially about the tree.

54
00:04:13,723 --> 00:04:15,723
Oh, you mean the world tree?

55
00:04:17,303 --> 00:04:18,133
Yeah, sure.

56
00:04:18,303 --> 00:04:21,774
I might not look like it, but
I know a lot about this game.

57
00:04:22,123 --> 00:04:24,620
There's this neutral
village to the north of us.

58
00:04:24,703 --> 00:04:27,160
It's a little out of the
way, but we can fly there.

59
00:04:27,243 --> 00:04:29,283
Okay, but what about Sylvain?

60
00:04:29,483 --> 00:04:31,189
Isn't that town closer to us?

61
00:04:31,663 --> 00:04:34,320
You really don't know
anything about this game.

62
00:04:34,403 --> 00:04:36,683
Sylvain is Sylph territory. So?

63
00:04:37,063 --> 00:04:38,100
You're not a sylph.

64
00:04:38,183 --> 00:04:40,220
If you're in their territory,
you can't attack them.

65
00:04:40,303 --> 00:04:41,723
But they can attack you.

66
00:04:43,183 --> 00:04:46,620
As long as I don't do anything to
provoke them, no one will attack me.

67
00:04:46,703 --> 00:04:48,585
And you'll be there, Miss Leafa.

68
00:04:49,923 --> 00:04:51,103
Just call me Leafa.

69
00:04:51,403 --> 00:04:53,880
And if you really want to
go there, I'll take you.

70
00:04:53,963 --> 00:04:56,198
I can't guarantee your safety, though.

71
00:04:57,103 --> 00:04:58,103
Let's get flying!

72
00:05:02,263 --> 00:05:05,557
Wait, you mean you can fly
without using the controller?

73
00:05:05,883 --> 00:05:07,223
Of course, can't you?

74
00:05:07,503 --> 00:05:11,400
I just learned how to use this thing, so
I'm still trying to figure everything out.

75
00:05:11,483 --> 00:05:13,895
Well, there's a little trick to doing it.

76
00:05:14,303 --> 00:05:17,100
Come on, turn around, but
don't access your controller.

77
00:05:17,183 --> 00:05:18,013
Okay.

78
00:05:19,303 --> 00:05:21,460
Can you feel where my
hand is touching you?

79
00:05:21,543 --> 00:05:22,373
Mm-hmm.

80
00:05:22,456 --> 00:05:26,140
Imagine you've got virtual bones and
muscles here spreading out into your wings.

81
00:05:26,223 --> 00:05:27,520
Then try and move them.

82
00:05:27,603 --> 00:05:29,423
Virtual bones and muscles.

83
00:05:31,703 --> 00:05:33,203
Yeah, just like that.

84
00:05:34,823 --> 00:05:35,823
You've got it!

85
00:05:36,303 --> 00:05:39,127
Okay, now try doing the
same thing, only harder.

86
00:05:46,863 --> 00:05:47,693
Ow!

87
00:05:54,983 --> 00:05:58,763
Oh, no! Daddy! Girito! Are you okay?

88
00:06:07,003 --> 00:06:09,183
How do I make it stop?

89
00:06:14,403 --> 00:06:15,815
Daddy, that's hilarious!

90
00:06:26,003 --> 00:06:28,683
Wow, this is awesome! I know, right?

91
00:06:30,023 --> 00:06:32,880
Looks like you're starting
to get the hang of it!

92
00:06:32,963 --> 00:06:35,303
Now, follow me! Okay!

93
00:06:35,943 --> 00:06:38,296
Take it slow until you get better at it.

94
00:06:39,663 --> 00:06:42,223
Don't worry about me, we can go faster.

95
00:06:43,943 --> 00:06:44,773
Okay.

96
00:06:56,283 --> 00:06:58,048
Is that as fast as you can go?

97
00:06:58,743 --> 00:07:00,743
Well, don't blame me if you crash.

98
00:07:13,183 --> 00:07:15,303
I can't go on, I need a break!

99
00:07:23,583 --> 00:07:27,465
You're the only person I know who
can handle flying at this speed!

100
00:07:35,483 --> 00:07:36,503
We made it.

101
00:07:37,583 --> 00:07:41,171
Hey, we're gonna land at the
base of the central tower, okay?

102
00:07:41,803 --> 00:07:44,943
Wait, Kirito, you do
know how to land, right?

103
00:07:46,443 --> 00:07:47,683
No, not really.

104
00:07:48,703 --> 00:07:50,823
Uh, oh crap.

105
00:07:51,263 --> 00:07:52,203
Too late now.

106
00:07:52,703 --> 00:07:53,963
You're on your own.

107
00:07:54,303 --> 00:07:55,183
Wait, what?

108
00:07:55,443 --> 00:07:56,743
You're kidding me!

109
00:08:04,563 --> 00:08:06,483
That was so not cool.

110
00:08:06,843 --> 00:08:08,160
Stop whining already.

111
00:08:08,243 --> 00:08:09,303
I can heal you.

112
00:08:10,303 --> 00:08:13,303
Zou, Vila, Heidel, Astolu.

113
00:08:16,303 --> 00:08:17,403
No way.

114
00:08:17,723 --> 00:08:18,823
This is magic?

115
00:08:19,163 --> 00:08:23,140
The Undine are the only ones who
specialize in high-level healing spells.

116
00:08:23,223 --> 00:08:26,600
But that's an important one anyone
can do, so you should learn it.

117
00:08:26,683 --> 00:08:29,212
Different races have
different skills, huh?

118
00:08:30,223 --> 00:08:32,620
Does the Spriggan race have
anything they're good at?

119
00:08:32,703 --> 00:08:36,409
Well, you guys are good at treasure
hunting and illusion magic.

120
00:08:36,643 --> 00:08:39,937
Neither of those things are
much help in battle, though.

121
00:08:46,343 --> 00:08:48,223
So this is a sylph town.

122
00:08:49,043 --> 00:08:50,403
Man, it's beautiful.

123
00:08:50,943 --> 00:08:51,963
I know, right?

124
00:08:53,263 --> 00:08:54,093
Lipa!

125
00:08:55,263 --> 00:08:56,703
Thank God you're okay!

126
00:08:57,423 --> 00:08:58,483
Oh, hey, Reckon.

127
00:08:59,663 --> 00:09:01,103
I knew you'd survive!

128
00:09:02,703 --> 00:09:03,533
Reckon!

129
00:09:04,803 --> 00:09:05,923
No, it's okay.

130
00:09:06,223 --> 00:09:08,282
He saved me from those salamanders.

131
00:09:08,883 --> 00:09:09,983
This is my friend.

132
00:09:10,203 --> 00:09:11,262
His name's Reckon.

133
00:09:11,943 --> 00:09:12,773
Hey there.

134
00:09:12,856 --> 00:09:13,863
My name's Kirito.

135
00:09:14,343 --> 00:09:15,183
Oh, hi.

136
00:09:15,403 --> 00:09:16,403
Nice to meet you.

137
00:09:17,523 --> 00:09:19,288
Wait, what am I talking about?

138
00:09:19,383 --> 00:09:20,280
I take that back.

139
00:09:20,363 --> 00:09:21,440
You sure about him?

140
00:09:21,523 --> 00:09:23,347
He could be a spy or something.

141
00:09:23,843 --> 00:09:24,843
No, he's cool.

142
00:09:25,203 --> 00:09:28,420
I'm pretty sure if he really was a
spy, he wouldn't be such a Tetsuo.

143
00:09:28,503 --> 00:09:29,823
Gee, thanks a lot.

144
00:09:30,423 --> 00:09:33,620
Anyway, Sigurd and the others are
waiting for you at the tavern.

145
00:09:33,703 --> 00:09:34,703
Oh, that's right.

146
00:09:37,463 --> 00:09:39,581
On second thought, I can't go today.

147
00:09:40,523 --> 00:09:41,353
Huh?

148
00:09:41,436 --> 00:09:42,463
You're not going? Nope.

149
00:09:42,743 --> 00:09:46,272
I sort of promised Kirito I'd
buy him a drink for saving me.

150
00:09:46,403 --> 00:09:47,233
See you later!

151
00:09:47,316 --> 00:09:49,343
Wait, you don't have to...

152
00:09:50,283 --> 00:09:51,683
Oh, Lipa!

153
00:10:04,643 --> 00:10:06,360
Is that retcon guy your boyfriend?

154
00:10:06,443 --> 00:10:08,040
Yeah are the two of you in love?

155
00:10:08,123 --> 00:10:10,140
No we're not in love.

156
00:10:10,223 --> 00:10:12,380
We're just in the same party is all.

157
00:10:12,463 --> 00:10:15,440
I don't know from where i was
standing you guys seem tight.

158
00:10:15,523 --> 00:10:18,240
Whatever i know him in
real life we go to the

159
00:10:18,323 --> 00:10:21,088
same school and we're
classmates but that's it.

160
00:10:24,583 --> 00:10:27,943
Anyway bottoms up and
thanks again for saving me.

161
00:10:32,623 --> 00:10:35,460
Those guys in the forest
were playing pretty rough.

162
00:10:35,543 --> 00:10:37,980
Are Gangs of PKers normal
for this game or what?

163
00:10:38,063 --> 00:10:41,300
Well, for one thing, the Salamander
and Sylph races never got along.

164
00:10:41,383 --> 00:10:45,380
But those guys were organized, and
that wasn't happening until recently.

165
00:10:45,463 --> 00:10:46,293
I don't know.

166
00:10:46,403 --> 00:10:50,040
If you ask me, they're gearing up
to try to clear the World Tree soon.

167
00:10:50,123 --> 00:10:53,480
Actually, I was hoping you could tell
me what you knew about the World Tree.

168
00:10:53,563 --> 00:10:55,504
Oh yeah, you mentioned it before.

169
00:10:55,623 --> 00:10:56,580
Why do you want to know?

170
00:10:56,663 --> 00:10:59,203
I want to get to the top as soon as I can.

171
00:11:00,543 --> 00:11:01,443
Join the club.

172
00:11:01,683 --> 00:11:03,500
Every player wants to get to the top.

173
00:11:03,583 --> 00:11:06,818
You could say that's the
grand quest of Alfheim Online.

174
00:11:07,103 --> 00:11:08,103
What do you mean?

175
00:11:08,643 --> 00:11:11,340
You know how you're limited
in how high you can fly?

176
00:11:11,423 --> 00:11:12,253
The fact is,

177
00:11:12,336 --> 00:11:16,140
none of the races can fly continuously
for more than 10 minutes at a time.

178
00:11:16,223 --> 00:11:17,053
However,

179
00:11:17,136 --> 00:11:21,864
at the top of the tree is the floating city,
and in it lives Oberon, the Fairy King.

180
00:11:22,323 --> 00:11:24,440
The first race to reach him will be reborn

181
00:11:24,523 --> 00:11:27,170
as an advanced class of
fairy known as Alphs.

182
00:11:27,463 --> 00:11:29,500
And what's cool about that is they'll be

183
00:11:29,583 --> 00:11:31,960
able to fly around for
as long as they want.

184
00:11:32,043 --> 00:11:32,923
That is cool.

185
00:11:33,363 --> 00:11:35,892
It'd be sweet to fly
for as long as I want.

186
00:11:37,183 --> 00:11:39,948
So how does someone get
to the top of the tree?

187
00:11:40,223 --> 00:11:42,600
At the base of the tree,
there's a big dome.

188
00:11:42,683 --> 00:11:44,780
That's the gateway to the floating city.

189
00:11:44,863 --> 00:11:49,628
But then you have to get past the NPCs
that guard it, and they're super powerful.

190
00:11:49,723 --> 00:11:51,194
They're that strong, huh?

191
00:11:51,623 --> 00:11:52,720
Let me put it this way.

192
00:11:52,803 --> 00:11:54,860
The game's been around
for a year now, right?

193
00:11:54,943 --> 00:11:56,323
No one's got past them.

194
00:11:57,063 --> 00:11:59,420
Maybe everyone's missed
that one key quest.

195
00:11:59,503 --> 00:12:00,333
No, wait.

196
00:12:00,603 --> 00:12:04,015
Maybe it's designed so that
one race can't reach it alone.

197
00:12:04,903 --> 00:12:06,763
Hey, you got good instincts.

198
00:12:07,103 --> 00:12:09,740
For now, everyone seems to
think it's a missing quest,

199
00:12:09,823 --> 00:12:11,260
so they're out there looking for it.

200
00:12:11,343 --> 00:12:14,620
But if we have to work together
to beat it, it'll never happen.

201
00:12:14,703 --> 00:12:15,533
Why not?

202
00:12:15,903 --> 00:12:17,668
Because it doesn't make sense.

203
00:12:17,823 --> 00:12:21,980
Why would you help another race with a quest
if they're the ones who get the reward?

204
00:12:22,063 --> 00:12:25,300
Can you imagine anyone being
cool with that arrangement?

205
00:12:25,383 --> 00:12:28,383
Then, getting to the top
of the tree is impossible.

206
00:12:28,663 --> 00:12:30,545
What's the point in even trying?

207
00:12:31,243 --> 00:12:32,543
No arguments here.

208
00:12:34,263 --> 00:12:36,322
Flying is pretty addictive, though.

209
00:12:36,483 --> 00:12:38,680
Once you get a taste for
it, you can't give it up.

210
00:12:38,763 --> 00:12:41,503
You think, even if it
takes years, someday.

211
00:12:41,843 --> 00:12:43,843
But I can't wait around that long!

212
00:12:50,523 --> 00:12:51,353
Daddy?

213
00:12:53,123 --> 00:12:53,953
Sorry.

214
00:12:54,123 --> 00:12:58,535
It's just that I have to get to the
top of the world tree as soon as I can.

215
00:13:00,463 --> 00:13:01,293
Okay.

216
00:13:01,376 --> 00:13:02,423
What's the rush?

217
00:13:02,663 --> 00:13:05,023
I'm sort of looking for someone.

218
00:13:05,603 --> 00:13:06,603
What do you mean?

219
00:13:07,483 --> 00:13:10,143
No offense, but it's hard to explain.

220
00:13:17,423 --> 00:13:18,480
Thank you, Leafa.

221
00:13:18,563 --> 00:13:21,269
All the info you gave
me is really gonna help.

222
00:13:28,083 --> 00:13:28,913
Wait.

223
00:13:28,996 --> 00:13:31,290
Are you heading for the
World Tree right now?

224
00:13:32,023 --> 00:13:32,853
Uh-huh.

225
00:13:33,023 --> 00:13:34,494
I need to see for myself.

226
00:13:37,723 --> 00:13:38,553
Alone?

227
00:13:38,683 --> 00:13:39,540
That's crazy.

228
00:13:39,623 --> 00:13:43,505
It's really far away and you'll
have to fight a bunch of monsters?

229
00:13:43,803 --> 00:13:45,440
I know you can handle yourself,

230
00:13:45,523 --> 00:13:51,323
but hey if you want I can take you there?

231
00:13:55,463 --> 00:13:56,293
Thanks,

232
00:13:56,376 --> 00:14:00,100
but we just met and I wouldn't feel
right you coming all that way right then?

233
00:14:00,183 --> 00:14:01,600
maybe you already know how to get there.

234
00:14:01,683 --> 00:14:04,095
What you're gonna do about the guardians?

235
00:14:04,183 --> 00:14:07,083
Well, I'll think of
something when I get there

236
00:14:08,043 --> 00:14:10,663
Too late my mind's made up

237
00:14:13,843 --> 00:14:14,673
Okay.

238
00:14:16,483 --> 00:14:18,601
So, do you want to meet up tomorrow?

239
00:14:18,823 --> 00:14:19,683
Yeah, sure.

240
00:14:20,123 --> 00:14:21,960
Then I'll meet you here
tomorrow at 3 p .m.

241
00:14:22,043 --> 00:14:22,873
sharp.

242
00:14:22,956 --> 00:14:23,992
Um, I have to log out now.

243
00:14:24,103 --> 00:14:26,980
So when you're ready, you can log out
in one of the rooms upstairs, okay?

244
00:14:27,063 --> 00:14:29,003
Well, see you then. Uh, wait!

245
00:14:33,783 --> 00:14:34,783
Thank you, Leafa.

246
00:14:43,303 --> 00:14:44,133
You

247
00:14:58,083 --> 00:15:00,663
Hey, if you want I can take you there?

248
00:15:09,883 --> 00:15:11,863
Talk about a weird guy!

249
00:15:14,343 --> 00:15:15,503
Hmm. Kirito.

250
00:15:25,723 --> 00:15:28,943
I guess this means goodbye
till tomorrow, doesn't it?

251
00:15:29,263 --> 00:15:30,840
Yeah, but I'll be back soon.

252
00:15:30,923 --> 00:15:32,217
It won't be that long.

253
00:15:34,983 --> 00:15:35,813
Daddy?

254
00:15:35,896 --> 00:15:38,263
Would it be alright if
I slept next to you?

255
00:15:38,643 --> 00:15:40,403
Just until you log out?

256
00:15:42,843 --> 00:15:45,083
Yeah, sure, I don't mind.

257
00:15:51,063 --> 00:15:53,360
You and me, we're gonna save Asuna!

258
00:15:53,443 --> 00:15:56,149
Then we'll all go buy a
house somewhere again.

259
00:15:56,643 --> 00:15:58,340
That would make me so happy!

260
00:15:58,423 --> 00:16:02,482
You know, living with you and mommy
again would be a dream come true.

261
00:16:05,863 --> 00:16:06,980
It's not a dream!

262
00:16:07,063 --> 00:16:09,603
I promise you I'll make it a reality.

263
00:16:21,543 --> 00:16:24,023
Good night, Daddy.

264
00:16:52,523 --> 00:16:56,170
Right now, your face is more
beautiful than anything, Titania.

265
00:16:56,943 --> 00:16:59,683
The way you look like you're about to cry.

266
00:17:00,563 --> 00:17:03,622
I wish I could preserve it
and hang it up on a wall.

267
00:17:03,863 --> 00:17:05,100
What are you waiting for?

268
00:17:05,183 --> 00:17:06,013
Permission?

269
00:17:14,003 --> 00:17:15,680
You can do whatever you want.

270
00:17:15,763 --> 00:17:17,200
I have no say in the matter.

271
00:17:17,283 --> 00:17:19,342
You're the system admin, after all.

272
00:17:19,983 --> 00:17:22,020
Such cold words from such a pretty mouth.

273
00:17:22,103 --> 00:17:26,338
Now, have I ever laid a hand on you
when you didn't want me to, Titania?

274
00:17:27,483 --> 00:17:29,600
Stop calling me by that stupid name.

275
00:17:29,683 --> 00:17:31,243
My name is Asuna. Sugo.

276
00:17:33,103 --> 00:17:34,643
You're spoiling the fun.

277
00:17:34,883 --> 00:17:37,824
In this world, I'm known
as Oberon the Fairy King.

278
00:17:38,163 --> 00:17:41,980
There's not a player who wouldn't give
everything to be the ruler of Alfheim.

279
00:17:42,063 --> 00:17:45,283
And you are Queen Titania,
my breathtaking bride.

280
00:17:45,683 --> 00:17:47,330
What more could you ask for?

281
00:17:47,803 --> 00:17:52,663
So, as my queen, as my bride, when
will you give your heart to me?

282
00:17:53,443 --> 00:17:54,273
Never.

283
00:17:54,503 --> 00:17:58,360
The only things I'll give you are
disgust and hatred, and nothing more.

284
00:17:58,443 --> 00:18:00,720
You're a stubborn girl,
I'll give you that.

285
00:18:00,803 --> 00:18:05,503
But you know, for a while
now I've been thinking.

286
00:18:06,063 --> 00:18:12,743
Romance is nice and all, but it might
be more fun if I just took you by force.

287
00:18:37,223 --> 00:18:38,183
Stop it!

288
00:18:43,203 --> 00:18:45,863
Of course, my dear. It was a joke.

289
00:18:46,143 --> 00:18:48,319
I'd never really force myself on you.

290
00:18:48,503 --> 00:18:49,803
I don't have to.

291
00:18:50,503 --> 00:18:53,463
You'll start wanting me
soon enough, I promise.

292
00:18:54,203 --> 00:18:55,303
You're insane.

293
00:18:56,603 --> 00:18:59,368
You won't be talking like
that for much longer.

294
00:19:01,343 --> 00:19:06,943
Right now, in this world, Tens of thousands
of players are enjoying this game.

295
00:19:07,303 --> 00:19:11,903
But none of them have a clue about the
true potential of the full-dive system.

296
00:19:13,063 --> 00:19:16,534
Did you know that by expanding
the brain's control regions,

297
00:19:16,663 --> 00:19:20,803
one could influence a person's
thoughts, emotions, and memories?

298
00:19:21,923 --> 00:19:22,943
You can't!

299
00:19:23,203 --> 00:19:24,980
Technology like that is illegal!

300
00:19:25,063 --> 00:19:26,323
Oh, but you're wrong.

301
00:19:26,783 --> 00:19:30,463
In fact, several countries are
researching it as we speak.

302
00:19:31,003 --> 00:19:35,123
The only thing standing in the way
is finding people to experiment on.

303
00:19:35,543 --> 00:19:38,955
But one day, I was watching
the news, and there they were.

304
00:19:39,643 --> 00:19:42,303
Ten thousand ideal guinea pigs!

305
00:19:45,103 --> 00:19:45,933
Mr.

306
00:19:46,016 --> 00:19:48,443
Kayaba was a genius,
but he was also a fool.

307
00:19:48,843 --> 00:19:52,003
All he wanted to use his
technology for was his game.

308
00:19:52,323 --> 00:19:54,441
He couldn't see the potential in it.

309
00:19:54,543 --> 00:19:55,663
But I did.

310
00:19:55,883 --> 00:19:57,940
It wasn't too difficult
to adjust the routers.

311
00:19:58,023 --> 00:20:02,160
The minute SAO's players were logged
out, I just grabbed a few from the flow.

312
00:20:02,243 --> 00:20:06,123
Just like that, I had 300 of
my very own test subjects.

313
00:20:06,663 --> 00:20:10,123
My research has taken great
strides the past two months.

314
00:20:10,303 --> 00:20:13,040
I've been developing a
technology that seeds memories

315
00:20:13,123 --> 00:20:15,829
with objects and uses
them to control emotion.

316
00:20:16,103 --> 00:20:18,223
My work is almost finished now.

317
00:20:19,543 --> 00:20:20,943
You are crazy.

318
00:20:21,223 --> 00:20:24,164
My father would never allow
that kind of research.

319
00:20:27,083 --> 00:20:29,700
He wouldn't if he knew
about it but it's being

320
00:20:29,783 --> 00:20:31,980
done in secret just a
small team and myself.

321
00:20:32,063 --> 00:20:37,500
Otherwise I wouldn't be able to sell
it off to who an american corporation

322
00:20:37,583 --> 00:20:41,400
you won't believe how Anxious they
are to get their hands on it and

323
00:20:41,483 --> 00:20:45,780
soon I'm going to sell it and wreck
to them for As much as I can that

324
00:20:45,863 --> 00:20:50,800
won't happen I'll see to that as
soon as I get back to the real world.

325
00:20:50,883 --> 00:20:53,942
The first thing I'll do is
report you to the police.

326
00:20:56,043 --> 00:20:57,063
You want to bet?

327
00:20:57,263 --> 00:21:00,145
You're in the same boat
as the other guinea pigs.

328
00:21:00,363 --> 00:21:02,220
What, you haven't figured it out?

329
00:21:02,303 --> 00:21:05,009
If I wanted, I could
alter your memories, too.

330
00:21:14,183 --> 00:21:15,203
I'm on the way.

331
00:21:15,563 --> 00:21:16,681
Wait for my orders.

332
00:21:17,963 --> 00:21:18,793
Don't worry.

333
00:21:18,876 --> 00:21:22,802
The last thing I'd ever want to do
is turn you into a porcelain doll.

334
00:21:23,263 --> 00:21:26,160
But the next time we
meet, I hope you'll be...

335
00:21:26,243 --> 00:21:28,603
just a bit more submissive.

336
00:21:30,163 --> 00:21:30,993
Titania.

337
00:21:46,603 --> 00:21:47,723
